## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design privacy-first OTCA paths that enforce data residency, tenant isolation, and masking, going beyond basic streaming.

## Key Concepts

- OTCA data contracts, regional immutable storage, global masked aggregates
- Per-tenant masking (tokenization, redaction) and tenant-key management
- Data lineage, access controls, and residency verification

## Code Example

```javascript
function maskRecord(record, tenantKey) {
  const masked = { ...record };
  if (masked.email) masked.email = hash(masked.email + tenantKey);
  if (masked.phone) masked.phone = redact(masked.phone);
  // redact other PII fields as needed
  return masked;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test masking correctness and residency under synthetic bursts?
- How do you handle schema evolution for masked fields across regions?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical OTCA telemetry design for AI inference with explainability, focusing on tenancy, privacy, and compatibility rather than volume. It requires mapping events, streaming paths, retention, and a lightweight schema-registry and tests, while introducing explainability data as a new angle.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-tenant AI telemetry
- Privacy-preserving ingestion (hashing, redaction)
- Per-tenant residency and retention
- Schema registry compatibility
- Basic QoS testing

## Code Example
```javascript
function redact(input){
  const crypto = require('crypto');
  const h = crypto.createHash('sha256');
  h.update(String(input));
  return h.digest('hex');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test backward/forward compatibility across schema changes?
- How would you implement per-tenant rate limits at the edge gateway?

