## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical understanding of lightweight, policy-driven OTCA telemetry for multi-tenant apps, emphasizing real-time decisioning, regulatory retention, and mobility across regions.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant residency and retention controls
- Ingestion-time redaction and field dropping
- Lightweight per-tenant policy engine with dynamic updates
- Edge-to-streaming architecture: edge gateway, regional Kafka, Parquet on S3 with tenant/date partitions
- Privacy, QoS, and policy-change verification

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo policy evaluator
function evaluate(event, policy) {
  if (policy.drop) return null;
  if (policy.redactUserId) event.user_id_hash = null;
  return event;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test policy updates without downtime?
- How would you monitor for privacy violations in production?

Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable OTCA path with privacy-first constraints, multi-region residency, dynamic redaction, and compliant purge workflows.

Key Concepts
- Per-tenant residency and data locality
- Dynamic, versioned redaction rules
- Immutable regional logs and global canonical events
- Canary rollouts and zero-downtime config reloads
- GDPR/CCPA purge and auditability

Code Example
```javascript
function redact(event, policy) {
  const out = { ...event };
  if (policy.redactPII && out.user?.email) delete out.user.email;
  if (policy.redactPhone && out.user?.phone) delete out.user.phone;
  return out;
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate purge requests across regions with clock skew?
- Which metrics indicate redaction misfires under load and how would you triage them?
